<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <!--
    Nop.Plugin.Tax.FixedOrByCountryStateZip - task 15.1
    (Requirements 5.5, 1.1-1.5, 2.4, 4.2, 4.3, 4.4, 5.1, 5.3, 3.1).

    THE RECIPE THIS FOLLOWS is the annotated
    src/Plugins/Nop.Plugin.DiscountRules.CustomerRoles/Nop.Plugin.DiscountRules.CustomerRoles.csproj
    (task 10.1). Read that file for the reasoning behind the five silently-failing decisions
    (Sdk.Razor + AddRazorSupportForMvc; the Content/Link block; Private="false" plus the
    NopPluginDoNotDeployHostAssemblies target; AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath=false; and
    Content Include - not Update - for non-.cshtml content). Only what is DIFFERENT about this
    plugin is documented here.

    ===================================================================================
    WHAT IS DIFFERENT (1) - THIS PLUGIN HAS ITS OWN DbContext (runtime deferral 4.10)
    ===================================================================================
    Data\CountryStateZipObjectContext.cs is an EF context of its own, registered by
    DependencyRegistrar through Nop.Web.Framework's RegisterPluginDataContext. It is the 4th and
    last of the four plugin contexts deferral 4.10 names (the others: task 11.2's
    Feed.GoogleShopping, task 13.1's Pickup.PickupInStore, task 14.4's Shipping.FixedOrByWeight),
    and it is why this project references Nop.Data DIRECTLY - the legacy project did too, alongside
    EF6 <Reference>s that are NOT restated here: EntityFramework 6.1.3 and EntityFramework.SqlServer
    have no place in this solution any more, and EF Core arrives transitively through Nop.Data
    (task 3.1). Its Install() now calls this.ExecuteSqlScript(CreateDatabaseScript()) - the shared
    GO-batch splitter in Nop.Data.DbContextExtensions (task 11.2) - not the single
    Database.ExecuteSqlCommand(dbScript) 3.90 used, which throws against the EF Core create script.
    See the class remarks in CountryStateZipObjectContext.cs.

    ===================================================================================
    WHAT IS DIFFERENT (2) - AN IStartupTask THAT USED EF6's Database.SetInitializer
    ===================================================================================
    Data\EfStartUpTask.cs called Database.SetInitializer<CountryStateZipObjectContext>(null), an
    EF6 static with NO EF Core counterpart (EF Core has no database initializers). Its body is now
    a documented no-op; the IStartupTask is KEPT so Nop.Core's startup-task enumeration is
    unchanged. See the remarks in that file.

    ===================================================================================
    DROPPED IN THE CLASSIC -> SDK CONVERSION (Requirements 1.4, 1.5)
    ===================================================================================
    As in the 10.1 template: ToolsVersion/DefaultTargets/xmlns, ProjectGuid, ProductVersion,
    SchemaVersion, FileAlignment, AppDesignerFolder, OutputType, TargetFrameworkProfile,
    NuGetPackageImportStamp, TargetFrameworkVersion v4.5.1, Prefer32Bit, ErrorReport,
    WarningLevel, DefineConstants and the Debug/Release DebugType/DebugSymbols/Optimize blocks;
    the explicit <Compile Include> list; the Microsoft.CSharp.targets import, the
    Microsoft.Bcl.Build.targets import and its EnsureNuGetPackageBuildImports guard, and the
    commented BeforeBuild/AfterBuild stubs.

    Every <Reference> with a HintPath into ..\..\packages\ is gone: the Microsoft.AspNet.Mvc
    5.2.3 / Razor 3.2.3 / WebPages 3.2.3 System.Web MVC stack, Autofac (transitive now),
    EntityFramework + EntityFramework.SqlServer (EF6, see above) and the net40/net45 polyfills
    Microsoft.Bcl.Async, Microsoft.Net.Http and Microsoft.Web.Infrastructure. The BCL <Reference>s
    are subsumed by the net10.0 shared framework, and <Reference Include="System.Web" /> has no
    net10.0 counterpart at all.

    app.config, packages.config and web.config are DELETED; web.config's load-bearing content is
    transcribed to Views/_ViewImports.cshtml. Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs is KEPT. Notes.txt stays
    non-deployed Content, as in 3.90.

    No <PackageReference>: this plugin has no third-party dependency of its own once EF6 is gone.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <AddRazorSupportForMvc>true</AddRazorSupportForMvc>
    <StaticWebAssetsEnabled>false</StaticWebAssetsEnabled>
    <OutputPath>..\..\Presentation\Nop.Web\Plugins\Tax.FixedOrByCountryStateZip\</OutputPath>
    <AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath>false</AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Required explicitly - Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor does not add it implicitly. The controller binds
    Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc (+ .Rendering for SelectListItem), the route provider binds
    Microsoft.AspNetCore.Routing / .Builder (IEndpointRouteBuilder, MapControllerRoute) and the
    tax provider binds Microsoft.AspNetCore.Routing (RouteValueDictionary, on ITaxProvider's
    GetConfigurationRoute).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Core\Nop.Core.csproj" Private="false" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Data\Nop.Data.csproj" Private="false" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Services\Nop.Services.csproj" Private="false" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Presentation\Nop.Web.Framework\Nop.Web.Framework.csproj" Private="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Private="false" alone is NOT sufficient - see runtime-deferrals.md section 83.3. This plugin
    references Nop.Data DIRECTLY, so Nop.Data.dll would be copied here by name rather than by
    transitive accident, and PluginManager would shadow-copy and load it as the process's
    Nop.Data. Verbatim from the template; the "Nop." prefix filter keeps Payments.PayPalDirect's
    private PayPal SDK working (task 12.3).
  -->
  <Target Name="NopPluginDoNotDeployHostAssemblies" AfterTargets="ResolveReferences">
    <ItemGroup>
      <ReferenceCopyLocalPaths
          Remove="@(ReferenceCopyLocalPaths)"
          Condition="$([System.String]::Copy('%(Filename)').StartsWith('Nop.'))" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

  <!--
    View resolution. %(Link) becomes the compiled Razor identifier, so the views compile as
    /Plugins/Tax.FixedOrByCountryStateZip/Views/*.cshtml and the controller's
    View("~/Plugins/Tax.FixedOrByCountryStateZip/Views/Configure.cshtml", model) call site stays
    UNEDITED (as do the two Html.PartialAsync("~/Plugins/...") sites). %(RecursiveDir) already
    contains "Views/" - do not repeat it.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Content Update="Views\**\*.cshtml"
             Link="Plugins\Tax.FixedOrByCountryStateZip\%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)"
             CopyToOutputDirectory="Never" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Runtime-read content, deployed exactly as in 3.90. Include, NOT Update - AND the <None Remove>
    first; under Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor the default Content glob covers only .cshtml/.razor, so a
    bare <Content Update="Description.txt"> would match NOTHING and PluginManager could not see
    the plugin at all.

      Description.txt   parsed by PluginManager.Initialize; SupportedVersions must contain
                        NopVersion.CurrentVersion ("3.90").
      logo.jpg          shown by the admin plugin list.
      Notes.txt         3.90 declared it Content with no CopyToOutputDirectory, i.e. not deployed.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Remove="Description.txt" />
    <None Remove="logo.jpg" />
    <None Remove="Notes.txt" />
    <Content Include="Description.txt" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
    <Content Include="logo.jpg" CopyToOutputDirectory="Always" />
    <Content Include="Notes.txt" CopyToOutputDirectory="Never" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
